      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex-supervisor): guard loadCodexSupervisorEndpoints JSON.parse against malformed env input",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using `OPENCLAW_CODEX_SUPERVISOR_ENDPOINTS` would receive a raw\n`SyntaxError` during startup when the value began with `[` but contained malformed JSON.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe endpoint parser now catches JSON decoding failures at its configuration boundary and reports\n`OPENCLAW_CODEX_SUPERVISOR_ENDPOINTS must be a valid JSON array.` Existing parsing for valid JSON\narrays, shorthand endpoint tokens, and the default local endpoint is unchanged.\n\nThe original standalone proof script was replaced with a regression case in the normal\n`codex-supervisor` Vitest suite so routine CI continues to exercise the failure path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed endpoint configuration now fails with a clear, actionable message instead of leaking a\nraw JSON parser exception.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: malformed bracket-prefixed JSON propagated a raw `SyntaxError`.\n- After: the same input throws the endpoint-specific configuration error.\n- Regression coverage: `extensions/codex-supervisor/src/supervisor.test.ts`.\n- Maintainer autoreview found no actionable defects in the production fix and integrated test.\n- Fresh hosted CI is running on repaired head `99025b96addef90cded02d7523a8c5a7a04fee2d`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/codex-supervisor-config-json-parse-guard",
